# <project> — night run rules

Owner's rulings for unattended overnight runs. Last reviewed: <YYYY-MM-DD>.

## 1. Base branch and merge policy

The branch stories start from and merge into, and whether the run may squash-merge
its OWN green PRs unattended, or must leave every PR open for the morning.

- Base branch: `<main|dev|...>`
- Unattended squash-merge of the run's own PRs: `<allowed|forbidden>`
- Never merged unattended, whatever the CI says: `<e.g. anything touching billing>`

## 2. Forbidden stories

Story ids the run must never pick up, each with the reason. PHASE B subtracts them.

- `<ID>` — `<why, e.g. needs a decision only the owner can take>`

## 3. Forbidden paths

Paths no night session may create, edit or delete, whatever the story says.
This section is ENFORCED, not merely written down: PHASE C turns every entry
below into an `Edit(<glob>)` deny line (and every secret into a `Read(<glob>)`
deny line) in the generated `settings.local.json`. So write each entry as a real
glob, repo-relative for paths inside the repo and with a DOUBLED leading slash
or a `~/` for anything outside it — `/x/**` alone is read as repo-relative and
would silently match nothing.

- `<.github/**>` — `<CI config is daylight-only work>`
- `<path/to/secrets/**>`, `<**/.env>` — `<credentials>`
- `<~/another-product-tree/**>` — `<not this project>`

## 4. Migration policy

How schema or data migrations may be produced at night, if at all — the ledger or
numbering authority that hands out migration numbers, and what is daylight-only.

- Migration numbers come from: `<path to the ledger, or "the owner, in daylight">`
- Forbidden at night: `<e.g. any migration that runs against live data>`

## 5. CI facts

Facts about this repo's CI that a session cannot infer and will otherwise get wrong.

- Required check NAME: `<the check that must be green>`
- Only this run event satisfies it: `<pull_request>` — a `push`, `schedule` or
  `workflow_dispatch` run does NOT count, however green it looks.
- Tooling quirks: `<e.g. "gh pr checks" fails with the configured token — read CI
  with "gh run list --event pull_request --json name,conclusion,headBranch" instead>`
- How long a story may wait for CI is NOT set here. It is `CI_WAIT_MINUTES` in
  `config.env` (default 45) — the runner reads config.env only, never this file,
  so a number written here would be silently ignored.

## 6. Post-merge invariants

Commands that must pass after every merge into the base branch. They exist because
something merged green and broke anyway. Name the command and what a pass looks like.

- `<command>` — pass = `<expected output or exit 0>`

## 7. Machine neighbours

Containers, ports, services and trees on this shared machine that this project must
never touch or restart. Cross-check `~/infra/INVENTORY.md` and `~/infra/PORTS.md`.

- Never stop or restart: `<container/service names>`
- Ports owned by others: `<port list>`
- Deployed tree — worktree/branch/tag operations only, never development: `<path>`

## 8. Resource floors

The minimum free disk in GB below which a run must not start, plus any other machine
limit this project is known to hit.

- `DISK_FLOOR_GB`: `<n>` — must match `config.env`
- Other known limit: `<e.g. the build cache grows ~N GB per build; hourly cap in
  ~/infra/systemd/disk-guard>`
